OL,3,GNEWSAWhat happens when a shoplifter is
OL,4,Abrought before the courts?
OL,5,
OL,6,FShoplifting has been described as a
OL,7,Fblight on UK high streets, costing
OL,8,Fretailers more than #2bn a year. Police
OL,9,Finsist it is a priority and have vowed
OL,10,Fto punish offenders. What happens when
OL,11,Fthey reach court? The BBC spent a day
OL,12,Fthere to find out.
OL,14,F"Good morning," shouts the prisoner on
OL,15,Fthe TV screen at Colchester
OL,16,FMagistrates' Court, as it crackles into
OL,17,Flife in August.
OL,19,FThe magistrates are facing their first
OL,20,Fdefendant of the day, 44-year-old
OL,21,FRobert Downey, who appears via a video
OL,22,Flink from prison.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
